<%#
  views/public/feed.ejs

  The home page: the news feed of live articles, with search, filters, sorting and
  infinite scroll. Open to everyone.

  How it is built:
  - The server renders the first 20 articles into this HTML (controllers/feedController.js,
    showFeedPage), so the reader sees articles immediately and the links are in the page
    source for search engines.
  - public/js/public/feed.js loads the next pages when the reader nears the bottom
    (IntersectionObserver), and reloads the list from page 1 when the search, a filter or
    the sort changes, all through GET /api/articles, without reloading the page.
  - A card here and a card built by feed.js have the same markup and classes (article-card),
    so they look the same however they were loaded.

  Why it is written this way (questions a lecturer may ask):
  - Semantic HTML5: main for the feed, aside for the sidebar (partials/sidebar.ejs), one
    article element per card, time with a machine-readable datetime, a form with role="search".
    Screen readers and search engines understand the page structure from these elements.
  - Flexbox layout: main-content-wrapper puts the feed and the sidebar side by side, and on a
    narrow screen stacks the sidebar below the feed (public/css/main.css), so the page works on
    a computer, a tablet and a phone (requirements: responsive).
  - Every text from the database is printed with the escaping tag (the one with an equals
    sign): a title containing "<script>" is shown as text and never runs (XSS). The tag with
    a minus sign is used only to include our own partials.
  - These notes are EJS comments (the tag with a hash sign): the server removes them, so
    they never reach the browser. An HTML comment would be readable by anyone with
    "View page source".
  - autocomplete="off" on the filters: otherwise, after "Back", the browser could restore a
    filter value that doesn't match the list the server rendered.
  - Every label is a real label element (visually hidden where the placeholder says enough),
    so screen readers announce each field.

  Rendered by: controllers/feedController.js (showFeedPage), for GET /.
  Locals: title, articles (feed cards: id, title, summary, imageUrl, category, reporterName,
  publishedAt, totalViews), hasMore (whether there is a second page), categories
  (Article.CATEGORIES).
  Includes: the shared head, header, sidebar and footer (views/partials).
  Owner: SH.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('../partials/head', { title: title }) %>

<body class="page-container">
    <%- include('../partials/header') %>

    <div class="main-content-wrapper">
        <main class="main-content">
            <h2 class="visually-hidden">Latest news</h2>

            <%# Search, filters and sort. No action or submit button: feed.js reacts to every
                change and the server is asked with fetch; Enter in the search box is handled
                by the script too, so the page never reloads. %>
            <form id="feed-filters" class="card feed-filters" role="search">
                <label for="search-input" class="visually-hidden">Search articles</label>
                <input type="search" id="search-input" name="search" class="form-field"
                    placeholder="Search articles..." maxlength="500" autocomplete="off">

                <div class="feed-filter-row">
                    <label for="category-filter" class="visually-hidden">Category</label>
                    <select id="category-filter" name="category" class="form-field" autocomplete="off">
                        <option value="">All categories</option>
                        <% categories.forEach(function (category) { %>
                            <option value="<%= category %>"><%= category %></option>
                        <% }); %>
                    </select>

                    <%# Viewed means opened from this browser (the deviceId cookie): readers don't log in. %>
                    <label for="viewed-filter" class="visually-hidden">Viewed or not</label>
                    <select id="viewed-filter" name="viewed" class="form-field" autocomplete="off">
                        <option value="">Viewed and not viewed</option>
                        <option value="unviewed">Not viewed yet</option>
                        <option value="viewed">Viewed</option>
                    </select>

                    <label for="sort-select" class="visually-hidden">Sort</label>
                    <select id="sort-select" name="sort" class="form-field" autocomplete="off">
                        <option value="newest">Newest first</option>
                        <option value="popular">Most popular</option>
                    </select>

                    <%# type="button": it must never submit the form. feed.js calls
                        DELETE /api/articles/viewed, then reloads the list (not the page). %>
                    <button type="button" id="reset-views-btn" class="btn btn-secondary">Reset viewed marks</button>
                </div>
                <p id="feed-action-message" class="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
            </form>

            <%# The list. data-has-more tells feed.js whether the server has a second page.
                aria-live="polite": screen readers announce new cards and messages. %>
            <div id="feed-list" data-has-more="<%= hasMore ? 'true' : 'false' %>" aria-live="polite">
                <% articles.forEach(function (article) { %>
                    <article class="card article-card" data-article-id="<%= article.id %>">
                        <span class="category-badge"><%= article.category %></span>
                        <h3 class="article-card-title">
                            <a href="/articles/<%= article.id %>"><%= article.title %></a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="article-card-meta">
                            By <%= article.reporterName %> |
                            <% if (article.publishedAt) { %>
                                <time datetime="<%= article.publishedAt.toISOString() %>"><%= article.publishedAt.toLocaleString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short', year: 'numeric', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' }) %></time> |
                            <% } %>
                            <%= article.totalViews %> views
                        </p>
                        <% if (article.imageUrl) { %>
                            <%# loading="lazy": images further down load only when the reader scrolls to them.
                                onerror: if the image's host is down or the link is broken, show our own
                                placeholder instead of a broken-image icon (this.onerror = null stops a loop
                                if the placeholder itself failed). The address was checked to be http(s)
                                when it was saved, and escaping keeps it inside the attribute. %>
                            <img class="article-card-image" src="<%= article.imageUrl %>" alt="<%= article.title %>"
                                loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; this.src='/images/placeholder.svg';">
                        <% } %>
                        <p><%= article.summary %></p>
                    </article>
                <% }); %>
                <% if (articles.length === 0) { %>
                    <p class="empty-state">No articles have been published yet.</p>
                <% } %>
            </div>
        </main>

        <%- include('../partials/sidebar') %>
    </div>

    <%- include('../partials/footer') %>

    <%# Order matters: feed.js and weatherWidget.js call apiClient, so apiClient.js loads first. %>
    <script src="/js/shared/apiClient.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/public/feed.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/public/weatherWidget.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
